[2026-07-14] Phase 4 — deploy & config hygiene (NOT pushed — awaiting approval)
Files: backend/Dockerfile, backend/config/settings.py, backend/requirements.txt, backend/core/migrations/0011_rename_*.py (new); deleted backend/Procfile, backend/railway.toml, backend/build.sh, backend/runtime.txt, backend/deploy_to_gcp.sh
Decisions:
- Dockerfile CMD now runs `python manage.py migrate --noinput` before `exec gunicorn`. Migrations are idempotent and, at min-instances 0, run only on cold start. Consequence: a deploy that carries a new migration applies it to the live Supabase DB automatically — this is exactly why the push/deploy needs explicit approval
- Reconciled the Django version: the venv AND the migration stamps were already 5.2.8 while requirements pinned 5.1.4 — prod was deploying a different version than dev tests. Bumped the pin to Django==5.2.8 (what the 25 tests actually validate). This surfaced a pending migration because 5.2 changed the auto index-naming algorithm; generated 0011 — a pure RenameIndex on ecopointshistory (ALTER INDEX ... RENAME, safe/fast). Deploying WILL apply this rename
- Deleted the four dead deploy targets (Procfile=Heroku, railway.toml=Railway, build.sh=Render, runtime.txt) and deploy_to_gcp.sh (duplicated the CI deploy, hardcoded the project id, and pushed the entire local .env — live Stripe/Cloudinary secrets — to Cloud Run). CI on push-to-main is the only deploy path now
- Removed the stale `*.onrender.com` CSRF origin (Render is gone) and the duplicate FRONTEND_URL definition

