- REAL BUG caught during Phase 1 verification, not by inspection: `@theme inline` only inlines --font-sans/--font-display into the Tailwind-generated utility classes (.font-sans, .font-display) — it does NOT emit them as standalone queryable CSS custom properties. My first fix, `body { font-family: var(--font-sans) }`, was silently invalid (verified via getComputedStyle showing Preflight's default stack instead of Geist) and would have been the exact same class of bug as the original Arial override. Fixed by referencing the raw next/font variables (--font-geist-sans, --font-fraunces) directly, which ARE present on <body> — confirmed body font now resolves to "Geist, Geist Fallback, ..." and a test .font-display element resolves to "Fraunces, Fraunces Fallback, ..." with the -0.03em tracking applied
- Purged all 8 token-immune hardcoded hex escapes (6× inline `#F7F1E3`, 2× framer-motion animate-prop literals in login.tsx) so they can't survive the redesign as beige artifacts; also fixed RippleText's stale base-03 fallback and its request for "Inter" (never loaded) to Fraunces (now loaded, self-corrects within a frame via the existing rAF loop so no fonts.ready wait was needed)
